---
/**
 * Public support URL for Station store listings.
 *
 * Play Console and App Store Connect need a reachable page, not just an email
 * address. This is listing infrastructure, not a marketing page. If you change
 * how someone reaches us about the Station app, change this page in the same
 * commit as the listing document in the Station repo.
 */
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '@/components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '@/components/Footer.astro';
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import Eyebrow from '@/components/Eyebrow.astro';

const updated = '18 August 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Station support — how to reach us · Kontour AI"
  description="How to get help with the Station app, where the privacy policy lives, and how to delete local data."
>
  <Nav />

  <Section contour size="hero" borderBottom>
    <div class="container container--readable">
      <Eyebrow accent="gold" gap="sm">Station support</Eyebrow>
      <h1 class="display-lg privacy-title">How to reach us.</h1>
      <p class="lead measure privacy-lead">
        Station is a local-first agent workspace from Kontour AI LLC. This page
        is the support URL the app store listings point at.
      </p>
      <p class="fine privacy-updated">Last updated {updated} · Kontour AI LLC</p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section borderBottom>
    <div class="container container--readable">
      <h2 class="display-md privacy-h2">Contact</h2>
      <p class="body measure">
        Email{' '}
        <Fragment set:html="<!--email_off-->" /><a href="mailto:hello@kontourai.io">hello@kontourai.io</a><Fragment set:html="<!--email_on-->" />.
        Include the app version (from Station's about or settings surface), the
        device OS version, and what you were trying to do.
      </p>
      <p class="body measure">
        There is no in-app ticket system and no Kontour-operated Station host
        you sign into. The app talks to a Station you run.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section borderBottom>
    <div class="container container--readable">
      <h2 class="display-md privacy-h2">Privacy and deletion</h2>
      <p class="body measure">
        What the app can collect, and the conditions under which anything
        leaves the device, are listed at{' '}
        <a href="/privacy/station/">/privacy/station/</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="body measure">
        Station's data is on your machine. Remove the app, or clear its home
        directory, and the local copy is gone. If you configured an endpoint
        that received telemetry or diagnostics, that store is yours or your
        operator's to clear.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section>
    <div class="container container--readable">
      <h2 class="display-md privacy-h2">The website</h2>
      <p class="body measure">
        Questions about this website, not the app, belong on the same address.
        The site's own collection policy is at <a href="/privacy/">/privacy/</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy-title {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
  .privacy-lead {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .privacy-updated {
    color: var(--color-chalk-3);
  }
  .privacy-h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
</style>
